Operational data, control boundaries and recoverable systems (@wu-water-ot: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Operational-Technology-Security-NIST.lingua#r_4W20M55VVPGFB1FAB00Q347KPT", #water-and-sanitation "Commissioning-acceptance-and-the-evidence-of-an-operating-service.lingua#r_6W0HRDKRCPBEVDR597P30KC9NB") { r_02ZS8WA9B122TABN9D1X1PQFM2
**Read:** [Operational technology security — NIST SP 800-82, revision 3](../sources/Operational-Technology-Security-NIST.lingua#r_4W20M55VVPGFB1FAB00Q347KPT) as the sustained security reference. Relate its methods to the fictional service developed here and the actual published process descriptions.

Map where measurements originate, where decisions run, who can issue commands, which network paths connect them and how the process continues when a connection disappears. Inventory includes configuration, calibration, clocks, credentials, firmware and tested restoration material as well as devices. A backup whose contents or restoration procedure are unknown does not demonstrate recoverability.

**Work:** Using a local diagram and synthetic data, distinguish read-only reporting from control authority. Describe least-necessary access, controlled changes, segmentation, logging and a verified restore sequence. Consider a stale historian value, duplicated command and unavailable remote service. Evaluate them through their effect on water, equipment and staff decisions.

Keep this investigation within public material or an explicitly authorized isolated system. For advanced study, restore a simulated service from a clean starting state and account for missing observations, controller state and manual work. Compare the cited final NIST edition with a later revision only after identifying actual changes; a draft's existence is not evidence that an operating requirement has changed.

**Return:** [Water, sanitation and industrial utilities](../Water-sanitation-and-industrial-utilities.lingua#r_7B9GRCJFHVBEEQEXKWCR2QMMPN).
**Continue:** [Commissioning, acceptance and the evidence of an operating service](Commissioning-acceptance-and-the-evidence-of-an-operating-service.lingua#r_6W0HRDKRCPBEVDR597P30KC9NB).

